hadiths[58]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16851","Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me from his book, he said: Hushaym narrated to us from Husayn from Muhammad ibn Talha ibn Rukana from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque."
"16852","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No one who severs kinship will enter Paradise."
"16853","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If al-Mut'im ibn Adi were alive and had spoken to me concerning these filthy ones, I would have released them for him, meaning the captives of Badr."
"16854","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I have names: I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Hashir, whom the people will be gathered at his feet, and I am al-Mahi, by whom disbelief will be effaced, and I am al-Aqib, and al-Aqib is the one after whom there is no prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"16855","He said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting al-Tur in Maghrib."
"16856","He said: Sufyan narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Babah from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Banu Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House or prays at any hour of night or day."
"16857","He said: Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: I lost a camel of mine at Arafa and went seeking it, and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing. I said: He is of al-Hums, what is he doing here?"
"16858","And Sufyan said once from Amr from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: I went seeking a camel of mine at Arafa and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing. I said: He is of al-Hums, what is he doing here?"
"16859","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at al-Khayf in Mina and said: May Allah brighten a man who hears my saying and retains it, then conveys it to one who did not hear it, for many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one more understanding than him. Three things over which the heart of the believer does not harbor deceit: sincerity of deed, sincere advice to the ruler, and adherence to the community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."
"16860","He said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Mis'ar, he said: Amr ibn Murra narrated to me from a man from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in the voluntary prayer: Allah is Most Great, Most Great, three times, and praise be to Allah abundantly, three times, and glory be to Allah morning and evening, three times. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his madness and his poetry and his pride. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are his madness and his poetry and his pride? He said: As for his madness, it is the epilepsy that seizes the son of Adam, and as for his pride, it is arrogance, and his poetry is poetry."
"16861","He said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us from Amr ibn Murra from a man of Anaza from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Allah is Most Great, Most Great, and praise be to Allah abundantly, and glory be to Allah morning and evening. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his madness and his poetry and his pride. He said: I said: What is his madness? He said: And he mentioned like the form of epilepsy, meaning fits. I said: And what is his pride? He said: Arrogance. I said: And what is his poetry? He said: Poetry."
"16862","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed me from al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the share of kinship from Khaybar between Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib, I came, I and Uthman ibn Affan, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, these are Banu Hashim, their merit is not denied because of your place which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, described you with, from them; what about our brothers of Banu al-Muttalib, you gave them and left us, though we and they are in one standing from you? He said: They did not separate from me in pre-Islamic times nor in Islam, and Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib are but one thing. He said: Then he interlaced his fingers."
"16863","He said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed me from al-Zuhri from Talha ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azhar from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qurashi has twice the strength of a man from other than Quraysh. And it was said to al-Zuhri: What did he mean by that? He said: Nobility of judgment."
"16864","He said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Abd Allah ibn Babah from Jubayr ibn Mut'im from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The best gift is this. O Banu Abd Manaf and O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, if any part of the authority belongs to you, then I shall surely know if you prevent anyone circumambulating this House at any hour of night or day."
"16865","He said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which lands are the worst? He said: And he said: I do not know. And when Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him, he said: O Jibril, which lands are the worst? He said: I do not know until I ask my Lord, Mighty and Majestic. And Jibril, peace be upon him, departed, then he remained as long as Allah willed him to remain, then he came and said: O Muhammad, you asked me which lands are the worst, and I said: I do not know, and I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, which lands are the worst, and He said: Their markets."
"16866","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Nafi' ibn Jubayr from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, descends every night to the lowest heaven and says: Is there any asker that I may give him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him? Until dawn breaks."
"16867","He said: Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey. He said: Who will guard us tonight lest we sleep through the Fajr prayer? And Bilal said: I will. And he faced the rising of the sun, and their ears were smitten, and nothing woke them but the heat of the sun. And they stood and made it up, then they performed ablution, and Bilal called the adhan, and they prayed the two rak'as, then they prayed Fajr."
"16868","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, descends every night to the heaven of this world and says: Is there any asker that I may give him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him?"
"16869","He said: Hasan and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyya, and one of them said: Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Hashir, and al-Mahi, and al-Khatim, and al-Aqib."
"16870","He said: Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Sulayman ibn Surad from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: We were discussing washing for major impurity with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I take three full handfuls and pour them upon my head, then I pour over the rest of my body afterwards."
"16871","He said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and became two parts, a part over this mountain and a part over this mountain, and they said: Muhammad has bewitched us. And they said: If he has bewitched us, he cannot bewitch all the people."
"16872","He said: Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to me from Jubayr ibn Mut'im from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: All of Arafat is a standing place, and keep away from the belly of Urana, and all of Muzdalifa is a standing place, and keep away from Muhassir, and all the passes of Mina are a place of sacrifice, and all the days of al-Tashriq are for slaughter. He said:"
"16873","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Musa from Jubayr ibn Mut'im from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it, and he said: All the days of al-Tashriq are for slaughter."
"16874","He said: Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Babah, the freedman of Al Hujayr ibn Abi Ihab, he said: I heard Jubayr ibn Mut'im saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Banu Abd Manaf, I shall surely know if you prevent a circumambulator circumambulating this House at an hour of night or day."
"16875","He said: Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Shihab mentioned from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father Jubayr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was addressing the people at al-Khayf: May Allah brighten a servant who hears my saying and retains it, then conveys it to one who did not hear it, for many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one more understanding than him. Three things over which the heart of the believer does not harbor deceit: sincerity of deed, obedience to those in authority, and adherence to the community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."
"16876","And from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr, the freedman of al-Muttalib, narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Huwayrith from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father with the like of the hadith of Ibn Shihab; he neither added nor omitted."
"16877","He said: Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from his father, he said: Muhammad ibn Jubayr informed me that his father Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed him that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke to him about something, and he gave her an instruction, and she said: What if, O Messenger of Allah, I do not find you? He said: If you do not find me, then go to Abu Bakr."
"16878","He said: Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me that Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im said: Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me that while he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him were the people, returning from Hunayn, the Bedouins clung to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him until they forced him to a samura tree and it snatched his cloak. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped, then he said: Give me my cloak, for if I had livestock as numerous as these thorn trees I would have distributed it, then you would not find me miserly nor a liar nor a coward."
"16879","He said: Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm al-Ansari narrated to me from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his uncle Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father Jubayr, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before revelation came down upon him, and he was standing upon a camel of his at Arafat with the people until he departed with them from it, by the guidance of Allah to him."
"16880","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'a informed me from al-Harith ibn Yazid from al-Harith ibn Abi Dhubab, if Allah wills, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head to the sky and said: The people of Yemen have come to you like pieces of cloud, the best of the people of the earth. And a man among those with him said to him: And from us, O Messenger of Allah? He said a subtle word: Except you."
"16881","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: al-Nu'man ibn Salim informed me from a man whom he named from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: I think he heard it from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people claim that we have no rewards in Mecca. He said: And I think he said: They have lied; your rewards will surely come to you even if you were in a fox's den."
"16882","He said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Idris from Husayn from Amr ibn Murra from Abbad ibn Asim from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he began the prayer say: Allah is Most Great, Most Great, three times; praise be to Allah abundantly, three times; glory be to Allah morning and evening, three times. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan, from his madness and his poetry and his pride. Husayn said: His madness is the epilepsy that seizes the possessed, and his poetry is poetry, and his pride is arrogance."
"16883","He said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama narrated to us from Zakariyya from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from his father from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no confederacy in Islam, and whatever confederacy there was in the pre-Islamic period, Islam only increased it in strength."
"16884","He said: Affan and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard one of my brothers from my father from Jubayr ibn Mut'im that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the ransom of Badr, Ibn Ja'far said: concerning the ransom of the polytheists, and he had not accepted Islam that day, and I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying Maghrib, and he recited al-Tur, and it was as if my heart was split open when I heard the Qur'an. Ibn Ja'far said: And it was as if my heart was split open when I heard the Qur'an."
"16885","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, informed me, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No one who severs kinship will enter Paradise."
"16886","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us from al-Nu'man ibn Salim from a man from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, they claim that we have no reward in Mecca. He said: Your rewards will surely come to you even if you were in a fox's den. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined his head toward me and said: Among my companions are hypocrites."
"16887","He said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the ransom of the people of Badr, and he stood and prayed Maghrib with the people, and recited al-Tur."
"16888","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed me from al-Zuhri from Talha ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azhar from Jubayr ibn Mut'im that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qurashi has twice the strength of a man from other than Quraysh. And it was said to al-Zuhri: What does he mean by that? He said: Nobility of judgment."
"16889","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed me from his father from Ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for something, and he said to her: Return to me. And she said: If I return and do not find you, O Messenger of Allah, hinting at death, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: If you return and do not find me, then meet Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"16890","He said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Jubayr ibn Mut'im narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not allot anything of the fifth to Abd Shams nor to Banu Nawfal as he used to allot to Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib, and that Abu Bakr used to distribute the fifth like the distribution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except that he did not give the kin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give them, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to give them, and Uthman after him, from it."
"16891","He said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Babah, he said: I heard Jubayr ibn Mut'im saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I shall surely know, O Banu Abd Manaf, if you prevent a circumambulator circumambulating this House at an hour of night or day."
"16892","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyya from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Hashir, and al-Mahi, and al-Khatim, and al-Aqib."
"16893","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I have names: I am Ahmad, and I am Muhammad, and I am al-Mahi, by whom Allah effaces disbelief, and I am al-Hashir, at whose feet the people will be gathered, and I am al-Aqib. Ma'mar said: I said to al-Zuhri: What is al-Aqib? He said: The one after whom there is no prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"16894","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No one who severs kinship will enter Paradise."
"16895","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father, and he had come concerning the ransom of the captives on the day of Badr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting al-Tur in Maghrib."
"16896","He said: Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Abd Allah ibn Babah informing from Jubayr ibn Mut'im from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), at the time of the bestowal of the gifts of Banu Abd al-Muttalib: O Banu Abd Manaf, if any part of the authority comes to you, then I shall surely know if you prevent anyone praying at this House at any hour he wills of night or day. And Ibn Bakr said: Circumambulating this House."
"16897","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im that his father informed him: While he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him were people, on his return from Hunayn, the Bedouins clung to him asking him and forced him to a samura tree, and it snatched his cloak while he was upon his mount, and he stopped and said: Return my cloak to me; do you fear miserliness from me? For if I had livestock as numerous as these thorn trees I would have distributed it among you, then you would not find me miserly nor cowardly nor a liar, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ma'mar erred in the lineage of Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Amr, and he is Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im."
"16898","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: I lost a camel of mine on the day of Arafa and went to Arafa seeking it, and there was Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing among the people at Arafa upon his camel on the evening of Arafa, and that was after revelation had come down upon him. He said:"
"16899","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed me from al-Zuhri, he said: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me that Muhammad ibn Jubayr said: Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me that while he was traveling with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith, meaning the like of the hadith of Ma'mar. He said:"
"16900","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us from his uncle, he said: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me that Muhammad ibn Jubayr said: Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me that while he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his return from Hunayn, and he mentioned its meaning."
"16901","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the road of Makkah, when he said: The people of Yemen shall come upon you as if they are clouds; they are the best of those on earth. Then a man from the Ansar said: And not us, O Messenger of Allah? So he fell silent. He said: And not us, O Messenger of Allah? So he fell silent. He said: And not us, O Messenger of Allah? Then on the third time he said in a faint voice: Except you."
"16902","He said: Waki and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: We mentioned ghusl from janaba in the presence of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: As for me, I pour over my head three times. And Abd al-Rahman said: Janaba was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: As for me, I take with my palms three times, then I pour over my head."
"16903","He said: Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, al-Numan ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: I heard a man whose name I do not remember narrating from Jubayr ibn Mutim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, people claim that we have no rewards in Makkah. He said: Your rewards will surely come to you, even if one of you were in the hole of a fox."
"16904","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyab informed me, he said: Jubayr ibn Mutim narrated to me that he came with Uthman ibn Affan speaking to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning what he distributed of the fifth of Hunayn between Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, you distributed to our brothers Banu al-Muttalib and Banu Abd Manaf and gave us nothing, while our kinship is like their kinship. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I only see Hashim and al-Muttalib as one thing. Jubayr said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not distribute to Banu Abd Shams nor to Banu Nawfal from that fifth as he distributed to Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib."
"16905","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Hammad al-Khayyat narrated to me, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite al-Tur in Maghrib. And Hammad said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited."
"16906","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Asim al-Anazi, from the son of Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, and Yazid ibn Harun said: From Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he entered prayer, and he said: Allah is Most Great, greatly, Allah is Most Great, greatly, Allah is Most Great, greatly, praise be to Allah morning and evening, three times, glory be to Allah morning and evening, three times, O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his hamz, his nafkh, and his nafth. Umar said: His hamz is madness, his nafkh is pride, and his nafth is poetry."
"16907","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz said: Shuba narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard one of my brothers narrating from my father, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, that he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning the ransom of the polytheists, and Bahz said: Concerning the ransom of the people of Badr, and Muhammad ibn Jafar said: And he had not become Muslim that day. He said: So I reached him while he was praying Maghrib, reciting therein al-Tur. He said: It was as if my heart split when I heard the Quran. And Bahz said in his hadith: It was as if my heart split when I heard the Quran."
"16908","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating that he heard Sulayman ibn Surad narrating from Jubayr ibn Mutim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that ghusl from janaba was mentioned in his presence, so he said: As for me, I empty over my head three times."
